[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
A fresh Kontrol-ID installation uses safe defaults and remains disabled until
it is enabled at Services > Kontrol-ID. Existing settings are preserved during
upgrades. The package manager installs the standalone multithread Kontrol-ID
engine and its exclusive policy GUI, including their dependencies.

Kontrol-ID cannot coexist with the conventional Squid or E2Guardian GUI/engine
packages because they own the same listener and policy paths. Remove the
conflicting products before installing Kontrol-ID.

Transparent identification maps source IPs to policies and never challenges an
intercepted browser. Transparent without identification skips the identity and
portal workflow and applies the default policy group. Explicit proxy mode
supports Kerberos/SPNEGO, Kerberos with NTLMv2 fallback, standalone NTLMv2 and
HTTP Basic for trusted networks.
Domain authentication uses the package-owned keytab and managed Winbind
service. Configure and validate them under Services > Kontrol-ID > Domain and
Keytab before enabling the respective method.

Endpoint enrollment is available only with transparent identification. It is
not required by transparent mode without identification. Domain join passwords
are sent only to kinit over a pipe and are never stored in config.xml.

Runtime databases in /var/db/kontrol-identity and protected domain state in
/var/db/kontrol-id-domain are intentionally preserved when the package is
removed. The standalone service is disabled by the package deinstall hook.
EOM
}
]
